    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-161861",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14158590/assets/759ebc78c794f433bba8c1f555bc68b2da52de62741711f13bd9c9156e3c485e.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=-2x,$ shown above. \nExpress the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14158590/observations/step-q161861-51af27137f280fb1044f.html",
